      "reason": "This directly governs rebuilding a Niño 3.4 anomaly from ERSSTv5, comparing it to CPC on specific 1991–2020 and 1981–2010 baselines, interpreting baseline offsets, and applying event logic on anomalies and ONI-style persistence without mixing seasonal definitions.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Rebuild Niño 3.4 from ERSSTv5 as monthly SST anomalies over Niño 3.4 (5S–5N, 170W–120W) relative to the stated monthly climatology for each baseline; match the published series baseline exactly (`base_period`), and state the climatology/baseline because the 1981–2010 and 1991–2020 series differ by a baseline offset, not different variability.",
        "For event counts use the operational persistence rule, not threshold crossings by eye: apply a 3-month running mean for ONI-style detection and require at least 5 consecutive overlapping 3-month seasons at or beyond ±0.5 °C (`min_duration` of `detect_threshold_events`); scan deviations on anomalies, not raw SST."
      ]
    },
